The engine

  nxnative, https://github.com/seedds/nxnative, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds.
  NX2Apple, https://github.com/LNPANDY/NX2Apple, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 LNPANDY and NX2Apple contributors.
  NX2Apple is a fork of nxnative that carries the patch queue, the launcher and the shell front end.

  Neither is vendored here. NX2Apple is cloned by hand into third_party/NX2Apple (or NX2APPLE_DIR), and
  tools/bootstrap.sh runs its own `tools/engine.py sync`, which materialises the engine tree from nxnative at the
  revision NX2Apple pins, then links it as engine/. The Mac launcher drives that tree. The iPhone app links none of it:
  each game's framework carries its own engine host (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

  What NXPocketApple reuses from them, and where:

  - The RomFS image identity (FNV-1a 64 over the header and the index, `romfs_id_of_image` in
    dm/host/romfs_identity.h). Reimplemented in core/Sources/NXPocketKit/Package/RomfsIdentity.swift, with tests.
  - The shape of `game.manifest.json` schema 1 and its validation rules (frontend-ios/Sources/ShellHost/
    GameManifest.swift). Reimplemented in core/Sources/NXPocketKit/Package/GameManifest.swift.
  - The launch environment and arguments a game's engine expects (frontend-ios/Sources/ShellHost/
    EngineLaunchPlan.swift and dm/ios/Sources/main.m's boot_env()). Reimplemented in
    app/Sources/NXShellHost/EngineLaunchPlan.swift.
  - The dlopen + dlsym + code-page remap the loader does (dm/ios/Shell/ShellMain.m). Reimplemented in
    app/Sources/NXShellHost/FrameworkLoader.swift.
  - The shell side of a game start (dm_shell_start_game and dm_shell_present_game in dm/ios/Shell/ShellMain.m, the
    entry points of dm/ios/Shell/ShellGlue.h, the scene's focus events). Reimplemented in
    app/Sources/NXShellHost/EngineHost.swift.
  - The probe that decided this project's architecture (probe/, from dm/ios/probe). Kept in this repository as the
    evidence docs/SIGNING.md cites.

The signing engine

  zsign, https://github.com/zhlynn/zsign, MIT, Copyright (c) 2018-2024 zhlynn.

  It is not vendored: tools/build_zsign.sh fetches it at a pinned revision, checks that its LICENSE really is MIT
  before compiling anything, and builds tools/zsign_shim.cpp against it into app/Signing/libnxzsign.a. Until that has
  been run, the app imports and verifies games and refuses to sign one.

  zsign needs OpenSSL. OpenSSL 3 is Apache-2.0, compatible with this project's MIT licence. build_zsign.sh takes
  the prebuilt iOS slices of https://github.com/krzyzanowskim/OpenSSL at tag 3.6.5000 (OpenSSL 3.6.0), pinned by
  revision 0a6149bff4fb00921ce0ec1811f726b166638095, and checks that its LICENSE.txt is the Apache License.

SFTP in the iPhone app

  The network sources screen reads games from an SFTP server (docs/SHARING.md §9). Apple has no API for SSH, so
  the app links Citadel and what it is built on, all fetched by SwiftPM and none vendored. core/Package.swift pins Citadel
  exactly; the rest float inside the ranges Citadel's own manifest allows.

  - Citadel, https://github.com/orlandos-nl/Citadel, 0.9.2, MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Orlandos. SSH client and SFTP.
  - swift-nio-ssh, https://github.com/Joannis/swift-nio-ssh (a fork of Apple's, which Citadel needs), Apache-2.0.
  - swift-nio, swift-crypto (BoringSSL inside, under its own prefix: it does not meet the OpenSSL the signer links),
    swift-atomics, swift-collections, swift-log, swift-system, all Apple, Apache-2.0.
  - BigInt, https://github.com/attaswift/BigInt, MIT, Copyright (c) 2016-2017 Karoly Lorentey.
  - ColorizeSwift, https://github.com/mtynior/ColorizeSwift, MIT, Copyright (c) 2015 Michal Tynior.

  Nothing AGPL or GPL is among them. They are linked into the iPhone app only: the Mac launcher does not use SFTP, and the
  NXPocketKit library that both share does not depend on any of them (they live in the separate NXPocketSFTP target).

Fonts in the built app

  The engine stands in for the console's shared fonts with two files in the app's dm/font, both made by
  tools/build_app.sh from Noto Sans JP (https://github.com/google/fonts, ofl/notosansjp, pinned revision and SHA-256),
  SIL Open Font License 1.1, Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with Reserved Font Name 'Source'.
  standard.ttf is its regular instance; nintendo_ext.ttf holds controller-button icons drawn by
  tools/fonts/make_ext_font.py, copied from the NX2Apple engine tree (MIT), with letters from its bold instance.
  Neither font is committed. No Apple font is copied into the app.

Nothing else is vendored but tools/fonts/make_ext_font.py. No key, no firmware, no game file and no extracted game data is part of this repository,
its tests or its fixtures.
